      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 884483172,
      "version": 1256,
      "versionNonce": 1512677141,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793281092980,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Threads are launched in whole blocks, so the grid always covers a bit more than\nthe data (div_ceil per direction). \n\nThe checks `col < width` and `row < height` switch the extra threads off.\nThat check is an `if` so it can split a warp. \n\nA: a vertical cut crosses every warp of the last column blocks.\nB: a horizontal cut crosses only the warp whos two rows sit on\neither side of it.\nC: both the width cut already makes all warps diverge, the height\ncut only leaves the bottom warp with fewer active threads.\n\nAlways ONE pass with idle threads, never a second pass: the \"no\" side\nhas nothing to run. Cost = idle cores in that one pass, few\nwarps only.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Threads are launched in whole blocks, so the grid always covers a bit more than\nthe data (div_ceil per direction). \n\nThe checks `col < width` and `row < height` switch the extra threads off.\nThat check is an `if` so it can split a warp. \n\nA: a vertical cut crosses every warp of the last column blocks.\nB: a horizontal cut crosses only the warp whos two rows sit on\neither side of it.\nC: both the width cut already makes all warps diverge, the height\ncut only leaves the bottom warp with fewer active threads.\n\nAlways ONE pass with idle threads, never a second pass: the \"no\" side\nhas nothing to run. Cost = idle cores in that one pass, few\nwarps only.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
